  <div v-else-if="item.kind === 'questions'" class="questions-scene"><div><div class="question-topics"><button @click.stop="emit('go', 'proof-details')">What is inside a proof? ↗</button><button @click.stop="emit('go', 'circuit-audit')">Who checks the circuit? ↗</button><button @click.stop="emit('go', 'statement')">Statement and witness ↗</button><button @click.stop="emit('go', 'pipes')">What about the peg? ↗</button></div><p>Clara Shikhelman · Mikhail Komarov · Aleksei Moskvin</p><span class="muted">Shielded Bitcoin: Private Transfers on the Bitcoin L1 · 24 Sep 2026</span></div><a :href="sources.sb.url" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><img src="/paper-qr.svg" alt="QR code linking to the Shielded Bitcoin paper" /><span>Read the paper</span></a></div>



  <div v-else-if="item.kind === 'proof-details'" class="proof-detail-scene"><div class="three-panels"><section class="violet"><small>PROOF ENCODING</small><h3>Curve points</h3><p>Three serialized points.<br />About 192 bytes in the paper’s profile.</p></section><section class="cyan" :class="on(1)"><small>GROTH16 VERIFIER</small><h3>Pairing check</h3><p>Proof points, public inputs<br />and the circuit’s verifying key</p></section><section class="amber" :class="on(2)"><small>ZERO KNOWLEDGE</small><h3>Randomized proof</h3><p>No readable private wires,<br />note openings or paths</p></section></div><p class="micro">The verifier must validate encodings and curve/subgroup membership as required by the chosen profile.</p></div>

  <div v-else-if="item.kind === 'circuit-audit'" class="audit-scene"><div class="audit-stack"><div :class="on(1)"><b>1 · Specification</b><span>Which attacks must the system rule out?</span></div><div :class="on(2)"><b>2 · Circuit implementation</b><span>Do the actual constraints rule out each attack?</span></div><div :class="on(3)"><b>3 · Verification artifacts</b><span>Do the build, setup and verifying key match that circuit?</span></div></div><div class="audit-examples"><small>ADVERSARIAL TESTS</small><p>Change the amount · path · key · ciphertext · nullifier</p><p>Check boundaries, overflow and unconstrained inputs</p><p>Independent review, test vectors and reproducible builds</p></div></div>

  <div v-else-if="item.kind === 'statement'" class="fields-reference protocol-fields"><section class="cyan"><small>PUBLIC INPUTS</small><p><code>r_anchor</code> · <code>N, M</code> · <code>nf[]</code> · <code>pk_eph[]</code> · <code>ct_note[]</code> · <code>h_body</code></p><span>Accepted root, counts, nullifiers, output keys/ciphertexts and body digest</span></section><section class="amber" :class="on(1)"><small>PRIVATE WITNESS</small><p><code>sk_spend</code> · input openings and creation context · <code>pos</code> and Merkle paths<br />Output value, <code>d</code>, recipient <code>pk_d</code> and <code>rseed</code></p></section><section class="violet" :class="on(2)"><small>DERIVED INSIDE THE CIRCUIT</small><p><code>sk_nf</code> from spending authority; <code>ρ</code> and <code>sk_eph</code> from <code>rseed</code><br />Input leaves and nullifiers are reconstructed and constrained</p></section></div>

  <div v-else-if="item.kind === 'keys'" class="view-access"><div class="three-panels"><section class="cyan" :class="on(1)"><small>INCOMING VIEW</small><h3><code>vk_in → sk_view</code></h3><p>Derive the incoming decryption capability</p></section><section class="cyan" :class="on(2)"><small>OUTGOING RECOVERY</small><h3><code>vk_out</code></h3><p>Decrypt sent-output recovery records in ct_out</p></section><section class="amber" :class="on(3)"><small>SPENDING AUTHORITY</small><h3><code>sk_spend</code></h3><p>Derive input ownership and nullifier secrets in the circuit</p></section></div><div class="wide-note">sk_nf alone cannot authorize a spend. Viewing keys are read-only.</div></div>

  <div v-else-if="item.kind === 'bytes'" class="cost-scene"><div class="metric violet"><strong>610<span>B</span></strong><p>Example transfer envelope</p><small>includes the proof and encrypted data</small></div><div class="metric cyan" :class="on(1)"><strong>625<span>vB</span></strong><p>OP_RETURN output</p><small>contribution, not the whole transaction</small></div><div class="metric orange" :class="on(2)"><i class="i-ph-sliders-duotone" /><h3>Policy matters</h3><p>Relay and mining rules</p><small>not a consensus change</small></div></div>

  <div v-else-if="item.kind === 'pipes'" class="pipes-scene"><div class="pipe-steps"><section><span>01</span><h3>Encrypted key</h3><p>A Bitcoin key locked<br />to a condition</p></section><section :class="on(1)"><span>02</span><h3>Condition met</h3><p>Allows the key<br />to be recovered</p></section><section :class="on(2)"><span>03</span><h3>Ordinary signature</h3><p>Bitcoin verifies<br />Schnorr</p></section></div><div class="attack-status" :class="on(3)"><i class="i-ph-info-duotone" /><div><strong>Once released, the key can sign arbitrary messages.</strong><p>Key release alone does not enforce a persistent covenant on future signatures.</p></div></div></div>

  <div v-else-if="item.kind === 'faq'" class="faq-scene"><div :class="on(1)"><h3>Does Bob need to be online?</h3><p>Not for the basic transfer. He can discover the output later by scanning the history.</p></div><div :class="on(2)"><h3>Can Alice tell when Bob spends?</h3><p>Knowing the plaintext is not enough. Alice does not have Bob’s nullifier secret.</p></div><div :class="on(3)"><h3>Can an indexer invent a balance?</h3><p>It can lie to a wallet that trusts it. The lie will not match independent replay.</p></div></div>

  <div v-else-if="item.kind === 'sources'" class="sources-scene"><a v-for="(source, key) in sources" :key="key" :href="source.url" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span>{{ source.name }}</span><i class="i-ph-arrow-up-right-bold" /></a></div>
</template>
